// Criterion: `&x` produces a `Ptr`; `*p` is the sole dereference form, reading the target value
// on the read side and writing through to the target on the write side.
// Treating `*p` as multiplication or failing to write through would leave `x` unchanged instead of `100`.
// Reference: 03-type-system/16-ptr.kv.
//
// ── Known limitation (excluded from active corpus scan) ──────────────────────
// **Blocked on pointer representation wiring**: `head.ptr` is still 0, layout does not emit `ptr=1`,
// and the encoder rejects capability rows with POINTER bits (`vmkv encoder: pointer and extension
// parameters are not representable from RWIR text yet`).
//
// Do **not** convert this into `// Expected error:` -- encoding an implementation gap as a negative
// test would enshrine a temporary limitation as normative behavior. Move back to `pointer/` once wired.
//
// Expected output:
//   42
//   100

rwfunc test() -> () {
	42 -> x:int64
	&x -> p:*int64
	*p -> q:int64
	println(q)
	100 -> *p
	println(x)
}
